Third-party components in the Docker image
------------------------------------------

go2rtc 1.9.15 - MIT License - https://github.com/AlexxIT/go2rtc
  Downloaded as a release binary at build time and verified by SHA-256 (see Dockerfile).

FFmpeg 7.1 (static build by mwader/static-ffmpeg) - GNU General Public License v3 or later
  The image contains the binary from the container image mwader/static-ffmpeg:7.1.
  Corresponding source: FFmpeg 7.1 at https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ and the build recipe at
  https://github.com/wader/static-ffmpeg (tag 7.1), including the sources of the libraries it
  links. DVR Bridge runs ffmpeg as a separate program; it does not link against it.

Python 3.13 (PSF License) and Debian bookworm packages from the official python:3.13-slim image.

Python packages (see requirements.txt for exact versions):
  FastAPI (MIT), Starlette (BSD-3-Clause), uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), httpx and httpcore
  (BSD-3-Clause), websockets (BSD-3-Clause), Pydantic (MIT), PyYAML (MIT), anyio (MIT),
  uvloop (MIT / Apache-2.0), httptools (MIT), watchfiles (MIT), python-dotenv (BSD-3-Clause),
  h11 (MIT), idna (BSD-3-Clause), certifi (MPL-2.0), click (BSD-3-Clause), tzdata (Apache-2.0),
  typing_extensions (PSF), annotated-types (MIT), typing-inspection (MIT), annotated-doc (MIT).
